# Jest tests

Test server behavior with Jest. A route or service is not done until it has test cases.

- Put tests in `server` as `*.test.js`, next to the module or under `__tests__/`.
- Run them with `npm test` (`node --experimental-vm-modules node_modules/jest/bin/jest.js`).
- Each feature needs cases for the success path, invalid input, auth or permission denial, and the centralized error code (`404`, `409`, and so on).
- Call the real function or the Express app. Mock only the database, clock, and outbound messages.
- Use a test database or mocks. Never point tests at production.
- Assert status, `code`, and the fields that matter. Do not assert full objects that include secrets or tokens.

```js
// ❌ BAD — no assertion
it('registers a child', async () => {
  await request(app).post('/children').send({ name: 'Asha' });
});

// ✅ GOOD
it('returns 409 when the vaccination already exists', async () => {
  const res = await request(app)
    .post('/children/1/vaccinations')
    .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`)
    .send({ vaccineCode: 'BCG', dose: 1 });

  expect(res.status).toBe(409);
  expect(res.body.code).toBe('VACCINATION_DUPLICATE');
});
```
